1 s; TT 29 / Mastery 232 (EIGHT sets) CORRECT first try with no generalize -- D24 kit mutations (M4A/AAC + FLAC\nunder `.wav`, thin LE-32 Mach-O, PE `0x0266`, ELF `0x0016`/`0x00b7`/`0x00f3`) were all parsed by the D23-generalized\nextractors. Flavor (unasked): \"Windows event logs from several hosts have been duplicated, truncated, and bundled\nwith reports. Count records accurately and find the selectively shortened timeline.\" -> siblings: EventRecordID gaps\n(selective deletion), header-vs-walk disagreement (dirty/truncated), duplicate logs across hosts (Computer), exported\n\"reports\" (CSV/XML) whose count differs from the binary.\n**D25 \"Hive Mind\" = REGISTRY HIVE** (`registry.hive_root_name` of one `hive-001.hiv`, 8192 B = 4 KiB base block +\none 4 KiB hbin; id `d25-registry-001-registry-hive-root-name`, `exact_text`/`trim`). Answer = the ROOT nk cell's name\nverbatim (base block u32 @0x24 -> cell 0x1000+off -> `nk`, name len u16 @nk+0x48, name @nk+0x4c, ASCII when flag\n0x20). DECOY: base-block FileName UTF-16 @0x30 (\"renamed\": single = truncated kebab path of the root name, timed =\nunrelated `<word>-<8hex>.hiv`). fmt word is the DOMAIN `registry`, not `regf` -> race MISS (lib had\n`regf.root_key_name`), live worker ~17 s, 0 wrong; TT 30 / Mastery 270 (NINE sets) first try, 2-3 s. Every D25 hive:\nseq1 == seq2, v1.3, root @0x20, flags 0x2c, 0 subkeys, 2 root values `Marker` (REG_SZ, single\n`HUNTRESS-HIVE-4203`, timed random hex) + `Ordinal` (REG_DWORD inline, 4203 = the marker's number) -- the unasked\n\"host labels\" for \"regroup the systems, and isolate the planted hive\".\n**D26 \"Before You Go\" = WINDOWS PREFETCH** (`prefetch.executable_name` of one `trace-001.pf`; id\n`d26-prefetch-001-prefetch-executable-name`, `exact_text`/`trim`). Single = `MAM\\x04` Xpress-Huffman-compressed (3896 B\n-> SCCA v30); TT + all 10 Mastery sets = UNCOMPRESSED SCCA v30 (~15.3 KB). Answer = SCCA header exe name UTF-16LE @16\nto the first NUL, verbatim uppercase with